From c2e8891150c54e4be46f6b44d79cfb84683d0e85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rdr-port <rdr-port@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:31:50 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/47] kernel: real XC_VIDEO flag values, widescreen switch;
 16:9 present of 720x480

- kernel.h: XC_VIDEO_FLAGS_* at their EEPROM values (0x00010000 widescreen,
  ...). The old 0x01/0x02 read as no flag after XGetVideoFlags' >> 16.
- xbox_VideoWidescreen / Set (RECOMP_WIDESCREEN): XC_VIDEO reports a
  widescreen TV only when asked.
- d3d11: a 720x480 frame with widescreen on is presented at 16:9; the
  window starts 854x480 then.
- glow skip: any reduced copy laid over a larger target (the scene is
  drawn into its own target, not the one the copy lands on).
- F2 menu: native widescreen row in place of the hor+ aspect.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
